# Facebook Comment Auto-Reply Bot

An AI bot that automatically replies to comments on your Facebook Page,
using Google Gemini (free tier) to generate friendly/professional/funny replies.

## How it works
1. Facebook sends a "webhook" to this bot whenever someone comments on your Page.
2. The bot sends that comment to Gemini, asking for a reply in your chosen tone.
3. The bot posts Gemini's reply back onto the comment thread automatically.

## Step 1: Deploy this code to Railway (free)
1. Go to https://railway.app and sign up (you can use GitHub or email).
2. Click "New Project" → "Deploy from GitHub repo" (you'll need to upload
   this folder to a new GitHub repo first — Railway will walk you through it),
   OR use "Empty Project" → "Deploy from local files" if offered.
3. Once deployed, Railway will give you a public URL like:
   `https://your-app-name.up.railway.app`

## Step 2: Add your Environment Variables
In your Railway project settings, go to "Variables" and add these 4:

| Variable name        | Value                                    |
|-----------------------|-------------------------------------------|
| VERIFY_TOKEN          | Make up any random string, e.g. `myBotToken123` |
| PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN     | Your long-lived Facebook Page Access Token |
| GEMINI_API_KEY        | Your Gemini API key                        |
| PAGE_ID               | Your Facebook Page ID                      |

Save, and Railway will redeploy automatically.

## Step 3: Connect the webhook on Facebook
1. Go to developers.facebook.com/apps → "Mypage Bot" → Products → Webhooks
   (if you don't see Webhooks in the sidebar, click "Add Product" and add it)
2. Click "Subscribe to this object" → choose "Page"
3. Callback URL: `https://your-app-name.up.railway.app/webhook`
4. Verify Token: the SAME string you used for VERIFY_TOKEN above
5. Click "Verify and Save"
6. Subscribe to the "feed" field (this covers comments)
7. Go to your Page's settings → make sure the app is subscribed to your specific Page
   (sometimes this needs a separate "Page Subscription" step under Webhooks)

## Step 4: Test it
Comment on one of your own Page's posts (from a different account/friend)
and watch — within a few seconds, your bot should reply automatically.
Check Railway's "Logs" tab to see what it's doing / any errors.

## Editing the bot's tone/personality
Open `index.js` and edit the `SYSTEM_PROMPT` text near the top —
that's the instruction that controls how it replies.

## Notes
- Never share your PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN, GEMINI_API_KEY, or App Secret with anyone.
- Gemini's free tier has rate limits — fine for a small Page, may need
  upgrading if you get a very high volume of comments.
- Facebook Page Access Tokens (even "long-lived" ones) expire after ~60 days —
  you'll need to regenerate one periodically unless you set up a System User token.
